# Fail rubric (~9 quality bar)

Treat work as **failed** if any of these apply:

- Business logic in controllers, route handlers, or React pages (belongs in services / hooks)
- Hardcoded user-facing UI copy (must use i18n keys)
- Access/refresh tokens in `localStorage`, `sessionStorage`, or JS-readable cookies
- Ad-hoc API error shapes (must be `ApiError`: `status`, `errorMessage`, `errorCode`, `errorKey`)
- New auth/error paths without tests
- Coverage below **80%** on touched `@repo/contracts` or auth modules (FE + Node + Python)
- `any` sprawl or unchecked deep imports across packages/modules
- New API errors without `errorKey` + i18n catalog entry
- HTTP routes outside `/api/v1/...`
- Cross-origin cookie auth without a documented exception
- New protected route without the role-check pattern (`RequireAuth` / `requireRole`)
- Critical POST (at least register) without Idempotency-Key support
- Production source maps enabled for the web app
- Secrets committed (only `.env.example` is allowed)
